e parenteral nutrition and enteral nutrition support services for numerous acute and chronic conditions, such as stroke, cancer, and gastrointestinal diseases; immunoglobulin infusion therapies for the treatment of immune deficiencies; and treatments for chronic inflammatory disorders, including crohn's disease, plaque psoriasis, psoriatic arthritis, rheumatoid arthritis, ulcerative colitis, and other chronic inflammatory disorders. It also offers treatments to manage the progression of neurological disorders, such as Duchenne muscular dystrophy, multiple sclerosis, Alzheimer's disease, and other neurological disorder; infusion therapies for bleeding disorders, such as hemophilia and von Willebrand diseases; therapies for women with high-risk pregnancies; and other infusion therapies to treat various conditions, including pain management, chemotherapy, and respiratory medications, as well as nursing services. The company markets its services through patient referrals, including physicians, hospital discharge planners, hospital personnel, health maintenance organizations, and preferred provider organizations. The company is headquartered in Bannockburn, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John Charles Rademacher | CEO, President & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $2.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $865K ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $33K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Option Care Health, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $4.7B market cap on $5.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years and +19% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 23% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $217M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.25\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 6.2\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 6.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Healthcare peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (46% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 23% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.5M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Option Care Health (OPCH) & Its Peers Head-To-Head Contrast","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/option-care-health-opch-its-peers-head-to-head-contrast.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794604525.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.932,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Option Care Health, Inc. $OPCH Stock Sold by Riverbridge Partners LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/option-care-health-inc-opch-stock-sold-by-riverbridge-partners-llc.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794396692.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.922,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Reviewing Wellgistics Health (NASDAQ:MEDS) and Option Care Health (NASDAQ:OPCH)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/reviewing-wellgistics-health-nasdaqmeds-and-option-care-health-nasdaqopch.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793906929.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.971,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Option Care Health (NASDAQ:OPCH) posts better-than-expected sales in Q3 2026","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/option-care-health-nasdaq-opch-131917611.html","dat